    "narrative": "For LawDog today, the top tier of our lineup is anchored by **Bryce Harper** (78.15) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19), both of whom offer the highest efficiency floors. **Bryce Harper** benefits from an elite xwOBA profile and a favorable matchup against Singer, while the +16% park factor adjustment for **Taylor Ward** against Peterson provides a significant boost, making him our premier outfield play. We are also leaning heavily into the matchup against Ryan Feltner; **Luis Arraez** (69.53), **Jung Hoo Lee** (66.57), and **Geraldo Perdomo** (65.99) are all projected to capitalize on his 4.62 xERA, further bolstered by wind-out conditions at the park. **Zack Gelof** (67.85) remains a priority start, as his matchup against Framber Valdez is mitigated by his high efficiency against lefties and the stolen base upside presented by Valdez\u2019s slow delivery.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **JJ Bleday** (51.32), who missed the cut despite a solid projection. While his platoon advantage against Luzardo was enticing, his low SP skill weighting against a pitcher of Luzardo\u2019s caliber ultimately made him the odd man out in favor of higher-floor assets like **Gavin Sheets** (63.23), whose favorable matchup against Merrill Kelly offers better run production potential. We are monitoring the status of **Tyler Freeman** (66.45) closely; while he projects well against Whisenhunt, the catcher framing factor remains a slight drag on his overall efficiency. All managers should note that while **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** and **Will Smith** remain sidelined on the IL, their absence continues to compress our depth, putting added pressure on **Jonathan Aranda** (56.90) and **Lawrence Butler** (56.10) to maintain our category production while we navigate these active lineups.",
